		"Amp: Level, Pan, Attack, Decay",
		"Isolator: Bass, Treble"
	],
	"notice": "Match the hardware MIDI channel and receive settings. Uses the factory multi-channel implementation: channels 1-10 select parts 1-10 and any note triggers that part. CC controls follow the selected part channel. The optional single-channel mode uses notes 48-57 and different CC assignments; remap before using that mode. USB MIDI availability and transmitted messages depend on mode.  GUI controls generate MIDI into the chain; route that chain to a MIDI output to control the hardware. DIN devices normally appear under the MIDI interface name, so select the profile manually. Unmapped physical buttons and switches have stable SVG IDs for future bindings. Positions are schematic. Note surfaces use virtual defaults; use MIDI learn to match the hardware octave or configuration.",
